#Student Course Registration System

#What the Project Does

The Student Course Registration System is a Python command-line application designed to help a school manage students, courses, and course registrations.

The system allows an administrator to:
- Add and manage students
- Add and manage courses
- Register students into courses
- View all students and courses
- View students registered in a specific course
- View courses a student is registered in
- Save and load data using JSON files

#Features Implemented
Add new students
View all students
Search for a student by ID
Add new courses
View all courses
Register students to courses
Prevent duplicate student registrations
Prevent duplicate student and course entries
Prevent course over-enrollment (capacity control)
View all students in a course
View all courses for a student
Save data to JSON files
Load data from JSON files
Input validation and error handling

#Classes Used
1-Person (Base Class)
Stores common attributes:
    name
    email
    phone number

2-Student (Inherits Person)
Adds:
    student_id
    Represents a student in the system

3-Course
Stores course information:
    course_id
    course_name
    trainer_name
    capacity

3-SchoolSystem
Core logic of the application
Manages:
    students
    courses
    registrations
Handles:
    adding data
    searching data
    registration 
    file saving and loading

#Challenges Faced
Making sure Object-Oriented Programming (especially inheritance) was used correctly
Avoiding students registering for the same course more than once
Making sure courses do not exceed their maximum number of students
Saving and loading data correctly using JSON files
Preventing the program from crashing when users enter wrong input